{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואתם הדבקים", :translit "v'atem hadevekim", :gloss "and you who cling"} {:he "תגין על הקו\"ף", :translit "tagin al hakuf", :gloss "tagin on the qof"} {:he "ק' ברכות", :translit "k' berachot", :gloss "100 blessings"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The numerical value of ק (qof) is 100, corresponding to the daily obligation of 100 blessings"}], :frame {:text "King David instituted the requirement to recite 100 blessings each day, as stated in Shabbat 35b. This is the one matter that David established by himself. The verse uses the singular form 'today' (היום) to hint that these 100 blessings are needed each and every day.", :sources ["Shabbat 35b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "כלכם היום", :translit "kulchem hayom", :gloss "all of you today"} {:he "וסמיך ליה למדתי אתכם", :translit "usmakh leilmedeti etchem", :gloss "and adjacent to it is 'I taught you'"} {:he "דשמעתא בעי צלותא כשמש", :translit "d'shemata b'tziluta k'mashma", :gloss "that the teaching requires prayer like the sun"} {:he "וזהו היום למדתי", :translit "v'zehu hayom limadeti", :gloss "and this is 'today I taught'"} {:he "שזכות הרבים הוא מסייעיתם", :translit "shez'chut harabim hu m'sia'atam", :gloss "for the merit of the many assists them"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word adjacency: כלכם היום is juxtaposed with למדתי אתכם in the next verse (Deut 4:5)"} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: היום ('today') links to the phrase היום למדתי ('today I taught') and the phrase בכל יום ('every day') from comment [0]"}], :frame {:text "The obligation of 100 blessings daily is derived in Shabbat 35b from the phrase 'today' (היום), teaching that it applies each and every day. The notion that the merit of the many is greater than the merit of the individual is discussed in Sotah 8a and expressed in the prayer text 'in the merit of the many' (Rosh Hashanah 4a).", :sources ["Shabbat 35b" "Sotah 8a" "Rosh Hashanah 4a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "The numerical v